guide forever/class/druid/bear-form
title Bear Form and Moonglade
category Class
folder Druid
keywords Bear Form, Teleport: Moonglade, Moonglade, Heeding the Call, Great Bear Spirit, Body and Heart, Moonkin Stone, Lunaclaw, Child of Nature, Great Ursera Spirit, Strength and Mercy, Ur'endra, Skyborne, class quest
reward spell 5487 "Bear Form"
why Your tanking form: Forever no longer trains Bear Form, these quests give it. Opens Moonglade too.
class Druid
levels 10-12
zone Moonglade

# Titled "Bear Form and Moonglade" (was "Bear Form & Teleport: Moonglade"):
# the guide casts Teleport: Moonglade, it does not give it; its Moonglade
# quests pay Cenarion Circle (and, for Skyborne, Nightclaw Druids) reputation and the
# Moonglade flight path, so the reward line names Bear Form only.
# The level-10 druid quests: Teleport: Moonglade and Bear Form. In Forever
# Bear Form is no longer trained: Body and Heart (6001 Night Elf, 6002 Tauren)
# and Strength and Mercy (94638, Skyborne) reward it (Forever's druid class
# quest list: "Rewards: adds Bear Form").
# - Night Elves: Heeding the Call (5923 Denatharion, 5924 Theridran in
#   Stormwind, 5925 Kal in Dolanaar: one of them) -> Moonglade (5921) -> Great
#   Bear Spirit (5929) -> Back to Darnassus (5931) -> Body and Heart (6001) at
#   the Moonkin Stone by Auberdine.
# - Tauren: Heeding the Call (5926 Innkeeper Pala, 5928 Gennia Runetotem in
#   Bloodhoof Village; 5927 Innkeeper Gryshka in Orgrimmar also leads to
#   Turak) -> Moonglade (5922) -> Great Bear Spirit (5930) -> Back to Thunder
#   Bluff (5932) -> Body and Heart (6002) at the Moonkin Stone in the pass out
#   of Mulgore.
# - Skyborne: Bear Form comes from Lotheluum Starbreeze on Zephras Isle (The
#   Great Ursera Spirit 94006, Strength and Mercy 94638). The Moonglade welcome
#   is Forever-new: Horde Skyborne get Child of Nature (94911) from Muln
#   Earthfury where the airship lands in Mulgore and Moonglade (94913) from
#   Turak Runetotem; Alliance Skyborne get Child of Nature (94912) from Alfina
#   Nightgaze beside the Skyborne Portal west of Dalaran (Archmage Ansirem
#   Runeweaver offers it too) and Moonglade (94914) from Sheldras Moontree in
#   Stormwind. Both reward Nightclaw Druids reputation (Forever's quest data).
# Left out: Stalk With The Earthmother (76156, 76160, 76240, Boarton
# Shadetotem in Thunder Bluff). Forever opened the three to every class
# (its change notes: "Classes none"; Tauren Warriors, Hunters, Shamans and
# Druids took them), so they are no druid quests: the chain is a Tauren side
# guide, forever/miscellaneous/stalk-with-the-earthmother.
# Places and gotchas from Forever's quest notes: the Great Bear Spirit
# (no quest mark, three trees, the talk is the objective), the right moonkin
# cave by Auberdine (the northern of two small caves; moonkin 11-13 outside,
# empty inside), Lunaclaw (level 12-13, three minutes, the spirit only after
# the kill; another druid's Lunaclaw counts too), the Barrens stone's level
# 20 Thunderheads, Ur'endra's unmarked cliff cave.
# The leveling guides carry all of this inline (nightelf/01-teldrassil,
# tauren/01-mulgore, both skyborne/01-zephras-isle; the Alliance Skyborne
# Moonglade welcome is proposed for them): this guide is for druids off our
# route.
# Sources: quests.json and npcs.json (Questie 12.1.0, Forever); Forever's
# quest data for 94911-94914; the skyboat points are the ones of
# collectibles/pets/shadowgale-squirrel.
# Druid flights out of Nighthaven: Silva Fil'naveth (npcs.json: Darnassus
# Flight Master, 44.2,45.2) flies druids to Rut'theran Village and Bunthen
# Plainswind beside her to Thunder Bluff, with no flight path needed (the
# Classic druid flights; another Forever 1-20 leveling route takes Silva's).
# The Night Elf and Alliance Skyborne steps of the druid guides send you to
# her instead of Sindrayl's two-leg flight by way of Auberdine.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Night Elves

step Heeding the Call
  only NightElf
  zone Teldrassil
  tip At 10 a druid's call reaches you: Kal in Dolanaar, Denatharion in Darnassus or Theridran in Stormwind. Any one of them sends you to Mathrengyl Bearwalker in the Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus.
  level 10
  accept 5925 optional                  -- Kal, Dolanaar; Denatharion's and Theridran's letters lead to the same place

# Mathrengyl stands upstairs in the druids' building and the walking maps have no way up inside it:
# without a waypoint the arrow led onto a ledge outside his floor, behind the wall (#1338). Each step
# to him comes after a goto at the building's door on its south side, 35.8,11.6, where players'
# recordings walk in; from there the arrow points straight at him.
step Cenarion Enclave
  only NightElf
  zone Darnassus
  tip Mathrengyl Bearwalker stands upstairs in the druids' building of the Cenarion Enclave. He teaches you Teleport: Moonglade with the quest (it stays in your spellbook, Balance tab).
  goto 35.8,11.6 "Cenarion Enclave"

step Mathrengyl Bearwalker
  only NightElf
  zone Darnassus
  tip Mathrengyl Bearwalker stands upstairs in the druids' building of the Cenarion Enclave. He teaches you Teleport: Moonglade with the quest (it stays in your spellbook, Balance tab).
  turnin 5925 optional                  -- or whichever of the three letters you carry
  accept 5921

step Moonglade
  only NightElf
  zone Moonglade
  tip Cast Teleport: Moonglade: it lands you beside the building where Dendrite Starblaze stands upstairs, past the armor vendor. The Great Bear Spirit sits in the woods to the north-west. Speak to it and go through all of its words (what it represents, the strength of the body, the strength of the heart, then ask for its blessing): the talk is the objective, there is no fight. It blends into the ground, has no quest mark and gives off a faint blue-grey glow by a group of three trees: from Nighthaven go west along the foot of the northern mountains, through the gap between the trees and the hills. If Dendrite is missing when you return, step outside and cast Teleport: Moonglade again. Learn the Moonglade flight path (Sindrayl, south of the lake) for later, then take Silva Fil'naveth's flight from the middle of Nighthaven: she flies druids straight to Rut'theran Village, no flight path needed. Take the portal up to Darnassus.
  turnin 5921                           -- Dendrite Starblaze
  accept 5929
  complete 5929 @39.1,27.5              -- Speak with the Great Bear Spirit
  turnin 5929
  accept 5931
  getfp "Moonglade"
  fly "Rut'theran Village"

step Cenarion Enclave
  only NightElf
  zone Darnassus
  goto 35.8,11.6 "Cenarion Enclave"

step Back to Darnassus
  only NightElf
  zone Darnassus
  turnin 5931                           -- Mathrengyl Bearwalker
  accept 6001

step The Moonkin Stone
  only NightElf
  zone Darkshore
  tip Fly from Rut'theran Village to Auberdine. The Moonkin Stone stands inside the nearest moonkin cave east of the village: the northern of two small rock-pile caves where the Auberdine road meets the main north-south road. Moonkin (level 11-13) stand outside, the cave is empty: slip past them. Use the Cenarion Moondust by the stone: Lunaclaw (level 12-13) walks in towards you and stays three minutes. Kill her, then speak to the Lunaclaw Spirit that appears and ask for the strength of her body and heart: the talk is the credit. Another druid's Lunaclaw gives you the spirit too.
  fly "Auberdine"
  use 15208 @43.5,46.0                  -- Cenarion Moondust
  complete 6001

step Body and Heart
  only NightElf
  zone Darnassus
  tip Fly back to Rut'theran Village and take the portal up to Mathrengyl.
  fly "Rut'theran Village"
  goto 35.8,11.6 "Cenarion Enclave"
  turnin 6001                           -- Mathrengyl Bearwalker: Bear Form

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Tauren

step Heeding the Call
  only Tauren
  zone Mulgore
  tip At 10 a druid's call reaches you: Gennia Runetotem in Bloodhoof Village or Innkeeper Pala in Thunder Bluff (Innkeeper Gryshka's letter in Orgrimmar works too). Any one of them sends you to Turak Runetotem on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff.
  level 10
  accept 5928 optional                  -- Gennia Runetotem, Bloodhoof Village; Pala's and Gryshka's letters lead to the same place

step Turak Runetotem
  only Tauren
  zone Thunder Bluff
  tip Turak Runetotem stands in the druids' hut on Elder Rise, over the rope bridges east of the lifts. He teaches you Teleport: Moonglade with the quest (it stays in your spellbook, Balance tab).
  turnin 5928 optional                  -- or whichever of the three letters you carry
  accept 5922

step Moonglade
  only Tauren
  zone Moonglade
  tip Cast Teleport: Moonglade: it lands you beside the building where Dendrite Starblaze stands upstairs. The Great Bear Spirit sits in the woods to the north-west. Speak to it and go through all of its words (what it represents, the strength of the body, the strength of the heart, then ask for its blessing): the talk is the objective, there is no fight. It blends into the ground, has no quest mark and gives off a faint blue-grey glow by a group of three trees: from Nighthaven go west along the foot of the northern mountains, through the gap between the trees and the hills. If Dendrite is missing when you return, step outside and cast Teleport: Moonglade again. Learn the Moonglade flight path (Faustron, south-west of the lake); Bunthen Plainswind in Nighthaven flies druids to Thunder Bluff.
  turnin 5922                           -- Dendrite Starblaze
  accept 5930
  complete 5930 @39.1,27.5              -- Speak with the Great Bear Spirit
  turnin 5930
  accept 5932
  fly "Thunder Bluff"

step Back to Thunder Bluff
  only Tauren
  zone Thunder Bluff
  turnin 5932                           -- Turak Runetotem
  accept 6002

step The Moonkin Stone
  only Tauren
  zone The Barrens
  tip The Moonkin Stone stands in the Barrens just south-west of Camp Taurajo, by the road out of Mulgore. Level 20 Thunderheads roam close by: clear the way first. Use the Cenarion Lunardust by the stone: Lunaclaw (level 12-13) appears for three minutes. Kill her, then speak to the Lunaclaw Spirit that appears and ask for the strength of her body and heart: the talk is the credit. Die in the fight? Lunaclaw stays by the stone: run back and finish her.
  use 15710 @42.0,60.9                  -- Cenarion Lunardust
  complete 6002

step Body and Heart
  only Tauren
  zone Thunder Bluff
  tip Back to Turak Runetotem on Elder Rise.
  turnin 6002                           -- Turak Runetotem: Bear Form

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Skyborne: Bear Form on Zephras Isle

step Skyboat from Dalaran
  only Skyborne,Alliance
  zone Alterac Mountains
  tip Bear Form is taught on Zephras Isle. Skip this if you are still on the isle; otherwise take the skyboat from the north side of Dalaran.
  goto 12.5,51.8 "Skyboat to Zephras Isle" live

step Skyboat from Thunder Bluff
  only Skyborne,Horde
  zone Mulgore
  tip Bear Form is taught on Zephras Isle. Skip this if you are still on the isle; otherwise take the skyboat from the cliffs south of Skywatcher Plateau, north of Thunder Bluff.
  goto 34.3,25.8 "Skyboat to Zephras Isle" live

step Lotheluum Starbreeze
  only Skyborne
  zone Zephras Isle
  tip Lotheluum Starbreeze stands in Valanaar.
  level 10
  accept 94006

step Urs'endris and Ur'endra
  only Skyborne
  tip Urs'endris waits by the waterfall below the Shrine of Akir, north-east of Valanaar. Ur'endra (the bear you must defeat) lairs in an unmarked cave high on the cliff face west of him, where the Shen'dar Highlands meet the Gustberry Lowlands: take the path west out of Valanaar (not north), cross the river on the log bridge and reach the cave from the cliff's upper, northern side. The cave at the foot of the cliffs and the foggy cave are the wrong ones.
  turnin 94006                          -- Urs'endris
  accept 94638
  kill 258443 quest 94638.1             -- Ur'endra

step Strength and Mercy
  only Skyborne
  tip Back to Urs'endris by the falls.
  turnin 94638                          -- Urs'endris: Bear Form

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Skyborne: Teleport: Moonglade

step Child of Nature
  only Skyborne,Horde
  zone Mulgore
  tip Muln Earthfury waits where the airship from Zephras Isle lands, in northern Mulgore beside Thunder Bluff.
  level 10
  accept 94911                          -- Muln Earthfury

step Turak Runetotem
  only Skyborne,Horde
  zone Thunder Bluff
  tip Turak Runetotem trains druids in the druids' hut on Elder Rise, over the rope bridges east of the lifts. He teaches you Teleport: Moonglade with the next quest (it stays in your spellbook, Balance tab).
  turnin 94911
  accept 94913

step Child of Nature
  only Skyborne,Alliance
  zone Alterac Mountains
  tip Alfina Nightgaze stands beside Denaaris Stargale and the Skyborne Portal, west of Dalaran, where the skycutter from Zephras Isle lands. Archmage Ansirem Runeweaver offers the same quest.
  level 10
  accept 94912 npc 270459               -- Alfina Nightgaze

step Sheldras Moontree
  only Skyborne,Alliance
  zone Stormwind City
  tip The Skyborne Portal takes you to Stormwind. Sheldras Moontree is the city's druid trainer (the arrow points at him); he teaches you Teleport: Moonglade with the next quest (it stays in your spellbook, Balance tab).
  turnin 94912
  accept 94914

step Dendrite Starblaze
  only Skyborne
  zone Moonglade
  tip Cast Teleport: Moonglade: it lands you beside the building where Dendrite Starblaze stands upstairs, in Nighthaven. Learn the Moonglade flight path while you are here (Faustron for the Horde, south-west of the lake; Sindrayl for the Alliance, south of it).
  turnin 94913 only Horde               -- Dendrite Starblaze
  turnin 94914 only Alliance
  getfp "Moonglade"
